<title>USA: Exxon restarts 88,000 bpd craker at Baytown, Texas.</title>
<headline>Exxon restarts 88,000 bpd craker at Baytown, Texas.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp restarted the 88,000 barrel per day (bpd) catalytic cracker at its Baytown, Texas, refinery, according to the company.</p>
<p>The cracker was taken out of service on Jan 23 for routine maintenance, according Bruce Tackett, company spokesman.</p>
<p>Total capacity for the refinery is 396,000 barrels per day.</p>
<p>--Matt Daily, New York Energy Desk +1 212 859 1626</p>
</text>
